  "Egyptian spices and hibiscus in copper bowls": "铜碗中的埃及香料和芙蓉花",
  "Egyptian tailoring, textiles and handmade crafts": "埃及裁缝、纺织品和手工工艺品",
  "Egyptian Tourism Authority": "埃及旅游局",
  "Egyptians have been baking, brewing and pickling on the same riverbank for five thousand years. Ful and taameya open the morning, molokhia and mahshi hold the family lunch, and hibiscus, sugarcane and mint tea close the night. The plates below trace the line from ancient jars and clay pitchers to the street classics visitors queue for today — a cuisine that never needed reinvention because it never stopped being cooked.": "五千年来，埃及人一直在同一条河岸边烘焙、酿造和腌制食物。富尔（Ful）和塔美亚（Taameya）开启清晨，莫洛赫亚（Molokhia）和马赫希（Mahshi）承载着家庭午餐，木槿花、甘蔗和薄荷茶则为夜晚画上句号。下面的菜肴追溯了从古代罐子和陶壶到如今游客排队品尝的街头经典美食的演变——这是一种从不需要彻底改造，因为它从未停止烹制的菜肴。",
  "Eight illustrated chapters that turn a national archive into something you can browse, plan a trip around and invest in. Every plate is documented, every era is placed, and every chapter connects to a live part of the platform.": "八个图文并茂的章节将国家档案转化为可供您浏览、规划行程和投资的内容。每个板块都经过记录，每个时代都得以呈现，每个章节都与平台的实时部分相连。",
