  "Location & Trip Tracking Policy": "Politique de suivi de localisation et de voyage",
  "Long before the 27 governorates, Egypt was 42 nomes, then Roman provinces, then Coptic bishoprics, then Islamic wilayat and Mamluk iqta'. The borders moved; the logic never did — the river organises the country. Read the ancient province map next to today's administrative divisions and the continuity becomes obvious: the same clusters of settlement, the same corridors, the same names surviving in modern towns.": "在27个省份出现很久以前，埃及曾是42个州，之后是罗马行省，然后是科普特主教区，再后来是伊斯兰行省和马穆鲁克伊克塔。边界在变动；但其内在逻辑从未改变——河流组织着这个国家。将古代省份地图与今天的行政区划并列阅读，其连续性显而易见：相同的聚居区、相同的走廊、相同的名称在现代城镇中得以保留。",
